Secret Management on AWS:
1- System manager parameter store
2- Secrets Manager
3- HashiCorp Vault (Not aws service)

If we store anything like docker credential to system manager --> parameter store then it is very easy to retrieve , we can just make a role for any service like codePipeline or for codeDeploy or codeCommit so these can access parameter store.

Now why i go for Secrets manager?

Now if you want to use rotation of certificate or password you should go with secret manager, like you have db credential or any certificate you must use secret manager. If your certificate can expire in 90 days you can automatically rotate it and also for db credential youc can rotate it in specific time according to need for security.
Secret managet provide different options like
rotation of secrets
You can custom lambda function to write logic of secret rotation

Now if you want to retrieve docker username and registry URL you can use System managet but if you want to use db credential or docker passord in your configuration you can use Secret manager. So if you use combination of both this is good.

Note one point that secret managet is expensive than system manager so you have to use it where it needs like we dont need it for registry url and usernames so must think for cost optimization as well.


